  "query_preview": "..Light to moderate showers continue across much of\nour CWA. Activity will persist through the early morning hours,\nwhich falls in line with our Flash Flood Watch remaining in effect\nthrough 5 AM MST. With many locations already saturated from\nthe wet Wednesday Arizona had, additional precipitation overnight\ncould cause flash flooding concerns. Remember to never drive\nthrough a flooded roadway or low-water crossing. \n\nAlthough our Flood Watch product expires early this AM, additional\nactivity is expected this afternoon, primarily across eastern \nArizona. Recent hi-res guidance runs suggest the White Mountains\nbeing the focal point for afternoon convection, but locations\nacross the higher terrain will all be susceptible to isolated\ncoverage of showers/storms. \n\nFriday through the weekend...The low pressure system across the\nPacific Northwest that's been assisting with the influx of\nmoisture into Arizona this week is forecast to push more inland\ntowards the upper Midwest. During this transition, shower and \nthunderstorm potential will become concentrated over our eastern \nborder, before pretty much dropping off completely by Sunday. \nWhile this disturbance is pushing eastward, a weak ridge will move\nover Arizona, aiding in the drier conditions as well as warmer \ntemperatures. \n\nNext week...Another disturbance looks to quickly roll in from the\nWest Coast, which may bring additional showers/storms mainly\naround Tuesday/Wednesday. Although confidence is still rather low\non how next week will shake out, so check back for updates.",
